                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The Burton of 1814 is essentially someone who Godwin is using to try and
                            raise funds and sort out his financial affairs - probably a lawyer, possbly
                            a money lender. The contacts take the form almost entirely
                            of Godwin calling - or sending Marshall to, or hearing from via
                            Marshall. THis may be Burton of Burton and Rist of 62 Conrnhill, who
                            dealt in the sale of lands.  'The particular friend' of the Irish Master of
                            Rolls, who is touted as a possible candidate for Serjeant (Morning Chronicle 25 February 1814) is likely the Burton Godwin meets in Ireland.</p>
